# =============================================================================
# RESEARCH MODES
# =============================================================================
# The engine defaults to DEEP research.
#
# Short research:
#   ./run_research.sh --mode short "your question"
#   ./run_research.sh --short-research "your question"
#
# Deep research:
#   ./run_research.sh --mode deep "your question"
#
# All workload values below are independently configurable for each mode.
# Most counts are PER RESEARCH TASK, not global totals.
#
# 1) *_MIN_CANDIDATE_PAPERS
#    Minimum unique scholarly candidates collected before a task can move on.
#    Higher values improve literature breadth but increase search/dedup time.
#    Practical range:
#      SHORT: 10-50
#      DEEP:  100-300+
#
# 2) *_DISCOVERY_TARGET
#    Early discovery target per task. Keep this above the minimum because
#    duplicates, weak records and filtering reduce the usable corpus.
#    Practical rule: about 1.2x-1.5x the candidate minimum.
#
# 3) *_PAPERS_TO_DEEP_READ
#    Number of top-ranked papers per task receiving expensive evidence-card /
#    deep-analysis treatment.
#    This is one of the largest local-LLM runtime drivers.
#    Practical range:
#      SHORT: 2-10
#      DEEP:  25-75
#
# 4) *_MAX_LLM_CONCURRENCY
#    Maximum simultaneous local LLM inference jobs.
#    Higher values may improve throughput but can cause VRAM/RAM pressure,
#    CPU offloading and severe slowdowns.
#    For RTX 5000 Ada 16-GB + Qwen3:32B:
#      1 = recommended
#      2 = upper practical range
#
# 5) *_MAX_TASK_CONCURRENCY
#    Number of research tasks allowed to run concurrently.
#    Higher values multiply LLM and network pressure.
#    For the 16-GB GPU:
#      1 = recommended
#      2 = upper practical range
#
# 6) *_SEARCH_QUERY_COUNT
#    Number of academic/search queries retained per task in discovery.
#    Higher values broaden terminology coverage and API calls.
#    Practical range:
#      SHORT: 3-10
#      DEEP:  10-30
#
# 7) *_WEB_QUERY_COUNT
#    Number of general-web queries retained per task/pass.
#    Practical range:
#      SHORT: 2-6
#      DEEP:  6-15
#
# 8) *_BLIND_QUERY_COUNT
#    Number of alternate-terminology / second-pass gap-search queries.
#    Practical range:
#      SHORT: 2-8
#      DEEP:  10-25
#
# 9) *_MAX_SEARCH_PAGES
#    Number of search/expansion pages used during discovery.
#    Practical range:
#      SHORT: 1-2
#      DEEP:  2-5
#
# 10) *_MAX_CITATION_HUBS
#     Number of high-value papers used as citation-expansion hubs.
#     Practical range:
#       SHORT: 2-5
#       DEEP:  8-15
#
# 11) *_MAX_WEB_RESULTS
#     Maximum web results retained for each configured web search call.
#     Higher values increase context and dedup work.
#     Practical range:
#       SHORT: 3-10
#       DEEP:  5-20
#
# 12) *_RUN_WEB_DEEP_READ
#     Whether technical/web pages receive additional deep-reading treatment.
#     Usually false for short research and true for deep research.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEEP RESEARCH SETTINGS - full workflow
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEEP_MIN_CANDIDATE_PAPERS=150
DEEP_DISCOVERY_TARGET=225
DEEP_PAPERS_TO_DEEP_READ=50
